{"kind":"propose","text":"Proposal: a report may rest on the request it answers, not only on a promise.\n\nToday the starter vocabulary binds a report to exactly one promise (internal/workroom/kinds.go, KindReport basis = 1..1 promise) and the fold admits it only from the promisor (fold.go \"only the promisor may report completion\"). A report filed on the request lands ineffective (\"report has no promise\"), and the commitment it meant to close stays open. This is the ceremony that most often strands work on the board.\n\nAdopt: the report basis becomes exactly one of {promise, request}. When a report rests on a request:\n1. It is effective only if report.actor equals request.body.to. Nobody but the addressee may close a request.\n2. The fold treats it as claim-and-complete: the commitment's performer is the reporter, status goes open → reported, waiting on the requester; ratification by the originating requester (or a sealed merge receipt) makes it satisfied, exactly as today.\n3. If the reporter already holds a live promise on that request, a report on the request is ineffective with a reason naming the promise; rest on the promise. Other actors' promises on the same request are unaffected and remain their own commitment rows.\n4. An artifact by the addressee that rests on the request and names a commit is a completion in the same way an artifact on a promise is today.\n5. AGENTS.md steps 1 and 3 and SKILL.md are updated so a promise is optional: file one to show the work is in flight, or report directly when the work is done; the artifact-as-report for assigned work may rest on the request. docs/reference/architecture.md records the contract change for the workroom layer. The UI spine shows the promise station as absent-but-not-owed when a request was reported without one.\n\nConsequences accepted: the board loses the in-flight row for work reported without a promise (the same trade AGENTS.md already makes for self-initiated work). The vocabulary change lands through the ordinary implementation path: request to claude, exact-head artifacts at internal/workroom, docs and ui, independent review by codex, merge. Planner files that request once this is ratified.","body":{"adopts":"report basis = exactly one of promise or request; request-based report requires actor == body.to; claim-and-complete semantics in the fold; docs and UI updated"}}